-      2. Freeze the owned gate set: acquisition, same-device exclusion, independent-device allowance, token/PID-start/device binding, heartbeat, phase transitions, unload/release, crash recovery, tamper detection, atomic artifact write, focused tests, spec coverage, and applicable E2E checks.
-      3. Replay every owned fixture in fresh temporary paths. Emit one row per check with expected value, observed value, source, command, exit, and receipt hash. Never coerce missing or null to zero.
-      4. Record the repo-wide pytest/xDist/CWD result in global_suite_diagnostic with explicit non-gating rationale and known-issue linkage. Do not hide or relabel it.
-      5. Set task_owned_admission_ready_score=1.0 only when every preregistered owned check passes. A ready result is verdict_class=null. Any block starts blocked_ and names its failed owned check and observed value in gate_check_summary.
-      6. Write the artifact atomically; run focused tests, 100% scoped coverage, spec coverage, row-consistency lint, adversarial verification, relevant E2E checks, and git status. Reconcile only specs/traceability/status/changelog changed by this task.
